 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Property of the affine compactification construction",
 "statement": "The constructed factorization $\\mathsf C_{\\mathrm{aff}}(U/S)$ is a\ncompactification of $U\\to S$. Consequently, if $U$ is a quasi-affine\nscheme and $U\\to S$ is quasi-compact and locally of finite type, then\n$U\\to S$ is compactifiable; this applies in particular when $U$ is affine.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-affine-cover/prop-nagata-affine-compactification.md",
  "place": "node prop-nagata-affine-compactification, order 312"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-affine-compactification",
  "def-nagata-compactifiable",
  "def-nagata-compactification",
  "def-nagata-relative-affine-space"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Since $U$ is affine, it is quasi-affine by\n[lemma-nagata-affine-finite-type-is-quasi-affine]. Apply\n[lemma-nagata-quasi-affine-immersion-affine-space] to obtain an\nimmersion $\\iota_U\\colon U\\to\\mathbb A^n_S$. Its composite with the\nstandard open immersion of\n[lemma-nagata-relative-affine-space-open-immersion] is an immersion\n$U\\to\\mathbb P^n_S$. By\n[lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-proper], $\\mathbb P^n_S\\to S$ is proper.\nThe immersion-into-proper construction of\n[lemma-nagata-immersion-into-proper] therefore supplies a\ncompactification, and this is exactly\n$\\mathsf C_{\\mathrm{aff}}(U/S)$ by definition.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-affine-finite-type-is-quasi-affine",
    "lemma-nagata-quasi-affine-immersion-affine-space",
    "lemma-nagata-relative-affine-space-open-immersion",
    "lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-proper",
    "lemma-nagata-immersion-into-proper"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
